  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6655898",
      "title": "Understanding Directives",
      "lectureOrder": 357,
      "videoOrder": 332,
      "sourceHash": "0973f7351a6c250daf101d4d58793c6ff3ef1bfca33a350e142741dd6813dae9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.52,
          "end": 5.64,
          "en": "-: We're almost done with the basics about Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.64,
          "end": 7.41,
          "en": "We learned a lot about components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.41,
          "end": 10.74,
          "en": "the basic building block of any Angular app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.74,
          "end": 13.2,
          "en": "about how it starts the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.2,
          "end": 17.25,
          "en": "how we can communicate with our templates in our components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.25,
          "end": 20.97,
          "en": "so that we can output data or react to events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.97,
          "end": 23.37,
          "en": "Now, there is one other key building block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.37,
          "end": 28.2,
          "en": "you probably use in any Angular app you build, directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.2,
          "end": 30.66,
          "en": "What are directives?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 33.87,
          "en": "Directives are instructions in the DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.87,
          "end": 37.29,
          "en": "and we actually already use directives without knowing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.29,
          "end": 41.19,
          "en": "Components are kind of such instructions in the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.19,
          "end": 44.31,
          "en": "Once we place place the selector of our component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.31,
          "end": 47.73,
          "en": "somewhere in our templates, at this point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.73,
          "end": 51.27,
          "en": "we're instructing Angular to add the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.27,
          "end": 53.34,
          "en": "of our component template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.34,
          "end": 55.83,
          "en": "and the business logic in our types of code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.83,
          "end": 58.56,
          "en": "in this place where we used the selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.56,
          "end": 60.157,
          "en": "This was our instruction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.157,
          "end": 63.63,
          "en": "\"Angular, please add our component in this place.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.63,
          "end": 66,
          "en": "And indeed components are directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66,
          "end": 68.46000000000001,
          "en": "but directives with a template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.46000000000001,
          "end": 72.15,
          "en": "There are also directives without a template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 76.71000000000001,
          "en": "So an example would be the appTurnGreen directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.71000000000001,
          "end": 79.83,
          "en": "which would be a custom directive we could build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.83,
          "end": 84.83,
          "en": "We typically add directives with attribute selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.87,
          "end": 87.3,
          "en": "but technically the selector of a directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.3,
          "end": 90.18,
          "en": "can be configured just like the selector of a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.18,
          "end": 93.84,
          "en": "So you could also use CSS classes or the element style,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.84,
          "end": 97.41,
          "en": "but again, typically you use the attribute style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.41,
          "end": 98.7,
          "en": "And on this paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.7,
          "end": 101.75999999999999,
          "en": "this directive might simply color the text green,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.75999999999999,
          "end": 102.9,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.9,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "So Angular would find this instruction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 108.96000000000001,
          "en": "Here, we would've defined our directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.96000000000001,
          "end": 113.07,
          "en": "with the directive decorator to inform Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.07,
          "end": 114.99000000000001,
          "en": "that this class holds a directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.99000000000001,
          "end": 118.71000000000001,
          "en": "And there we might have the logic to turn this green.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.71000000000001,
          "end": 121.77,
          "en": "Now we will learn how to write our own directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.77,
          "end": 125.85,
          "en": "in the section focused on directives in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.85,
          "end": 128.4,
          "en": "but there are a couple of builtin directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 130.29,
          "en": "which are really useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.29,
          "end": 132.36,
          "en": "Let's take a closer look at how we use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.36,
          "end": 135.093,
          "en": "and what they do for us in the next lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
